{"id": "DfTl32dRp1E", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "The day Parshurama challenged Lord Ram… and handed him Vishnu's own bow 🏹🪓 Part 6 of the Parshurama series.\n\nRam had just broken Shiva's bow and married Sita. On the road home to Ayodhya, birds shrieked, the sky went dark, a storm tore up the trees, and out of the dust came Parshurama, axe on his shoulder, a bow in his hand. The sages whispered: \"Has he come for the kings again?\"\n\n\"You broke Shiva's bow? String this one. Then fight me.\" King Dasharatha begged him to spare his sons, but Parshurama spoke only to Ram. Two bows had once been made: Shiva's, the one Ram broke, and Vishnu's, handed down from Rishi Richika to Jamadagni to Parshurama.\n\nRam took the bow, strung it and nocked an arrow. \"You are a brahmin, and Vishvamitra's kin, so I won't take your life. But this arrow never misses. Choose: your speed of mind, or the heavens your tapas won.\" As the gods gathered to watch, Parshurama's power left him. He knew Ram was Vishnu. \"Take my heavens. Leave me my speed.\" The arrow struck, he walked around Ram, bowed, and left for Mount Mahendra.\n\n📖 Source: Valmiki Ramayana, Bala Kanda 74–76.\n\n📚 Stories of Shakti for little ones: the Navadurga Set from Rishi Katha is out now. Check the link in bio (rishikatha.com).\n\n💬 Why couldn't Parshurama stay on earth at night? Comment if you know (answer pinned 👇)\n🔁 Save it for Part 7 and share it with someone who loves Ram and Parshurama.\n\n#parshuram #parshurama #shriram #jaishriram #ramayan #valmikiramayan #vishnuavatar #dashavatar #sitaram #hindumythology #sanatandharma #indianmythology #mythologystories #rishikatha #hinduism", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793766360, "like_count": 4419, "comment_count": 26, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1107438112063346a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 51.67, "asr": 48000, "format_n